# Web

## Naming Conventions

- Name controllers `*Controller` with a resource name (`HolidayController`, not `ApiController`).
- Name API payloads `*Request` and `*Response` records.

## Rules

- Annotate REST controllers with `@RestController` and a class-level `@RequestMapping`.
- Use method-level HTTP verb annotations for each operation.
- Return `ResponseEntity` with a typed `*Response` record for REST endpoints.
- Include a `Location` header on HTTP 201; build it with `UriComponentsBuilder` as a method parameter.
- Return 200 for GET and PUT; 200 with an empty collection when a list is empty; 201 with body for POST; 204 for DELETE; 404 when a single-resource GET or DELETE finds nothing.
- Apply `@Valid` to every `@RequestBody`. Apply `@Positive` to numeric `@PathVariable` identifiers.
- Map `Optional<T>` service returns with `.map(ResponseEntity::ok).orElseGet(() -> ResponseEntity.notFound().build())`.
- Delegate business rules to a feature service; keep HTTP mapping in the controller.
- Declare `*Request` and `*Response` as records in the feature package.

## Good vs bad

```java
// GOOD
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/v1/holidays")
class HolidayController {
  private final HolidayService holidayService;

  HolidayController(HolidayService holidayService) {
    this.holidayService = Objects.requireNonNull(holidayService, "holidayService");
  }

  @GetMapping("/{id}")
  ResponseEntity<HolidayResponse> getById(@PathVariable @Positive long id) {
    return holidayService.findById(id)
        .map(ResponseEntity::ok)
        .orElseGet(() -> ResponseEntity.notFound().build());
  }
}

public record HolidayRequest(@NotBlank String name) {}
public record HolidayResponse(long id, String name) {}

// BAD
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/holidays")
public class HolidayController {
  @Autowired private HolidayRepository holidayRepository;

  @GetMapping("/{id}")
  public HolidayEntity get(@PathVariable Long id) {
    return holidayRepository.findById(id).get();
  }
}

@Data
public class HolidayRequest { private String name; }
```

## Safety Guards

- Never call `Optional.get()` on a service-returned `Optional`.
- Never mix `@RestController` and page rendering in the same class.
- Never use `@RequestBody` on GET or DELETE.
